[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own reports say
otherwise. Read by tenant instead of by subject or intake tag, they split into three problems.
Each problem now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix will not close #4471. The booking-v3 form hint and the one-day moves
need fixes of their own.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: 'https://github.com/AdamZajler/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/1', hint: 'https://github.com/AdamZajler/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/2', 'one-day move': 'https://github.com/AdamZajler/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/3' }} />

- **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. Day and month swap.
- **hint**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as
  told, and the form reads the date day first. This happens only through the form, and only for
  booking-v3 tenants.
- **one-day move**: the date moves by one day, not by a swap. It looks like a timezone problem.
  The desk had already read these reports this way (desk notes).

## How this was counted

- One id, one report: the ticket export repeats some reports across pages.
- Cause by tenant (locale and booking form), with `causeOf` in `causes.ts`. The intake tag is a
  guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the tenant often enough that it can't be
  used for counting.
- The same split by the desk's own rule, with one-day moves counted under their tenant's cause:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes on the desk

- Do not merge a date report into #4471 on its subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  Check the tenant and the channel first, with the [triage explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe).

